### 5.1 Healthcare Claim Transformation Example

**Scenario**: Transform external claim events from clearinghouse to internal format with enrichment, validation, and routing.

**External Claim Event** (from clearinghouse):
```json
{
  "externalClaimId": "CLM-EXT-12345",
  "claimTypeCode": "PROF",
  "billedAmountString": "1250.00",
  "discountPercentage": 10,
  "serviceDateString": "2025-01-10",
  "statusCode": "SUBMITTED",
  "patient": { "id": "PAT-9876" },
  "provider": { "taxId": "12-3456789", "npi": "1234567890" },
  "posCode": "11",
  "diagnosisPointers": ["A01.1", "B02.3"]
}
```

**Transformation Pipeline**:
```csharp
// 1. Map external to internal format
var internalClaim = await _claimMappingTransformer.TransformAsync(externalClaim);
// Result: ClaimId="CLM-12345", ClaimAmount=1125.00 (after discount), Status=Submitted

// 2. Enrich with domain data
var enrichedClaim = await _claimEnrichmentTransformer.TransformAsync(internalClaim);
// Result: Added PatientDetails (name, DOB, plan) and ProviderDetails (specialty, network status)

// 3. Apply business rules
var validatedClaim = await _businessRulesTransformer.TransformAsync(enrichedClaim);
// Result: RequiresManualReview=false, FraudFlags=[]

// 4. Route to appropriate topic
var routedClaim = await _claimRoutingTransformer.TransformAsync(validatedClaim);
// Result: TargetTopic="claims.standard" (amount < $10k and in-network)
```

